# RS-009: Picker drops answers

> answers vanish and the card parks

## Symptom

%% @gummi: what goes wrong, in the requester's own words — what was seen, where, and how often

## Reproduction

%% @gummi: how to see it happen; when it cannot be reproduced on demand, say so and name what the evidence is instead

## Constraints

%% @gummi: the bounds of the investigation (time, scope, what must not be touched)

## Evidence

%% @gummi: what the investigation observed — prose with inline `path:line` / `path:start-end` citations

## Ruled out

%% @gummi: candidate causes eliminated, and what eliminated each — this is what stops the fix cards re-walking dead ends

## Causes

%% @gummi: the causes found — one bullet each, saying why it produces the symptom; a symptom with two causes gets two bullets

## Slices

%% @gummi: the follow-on work, one row per cause — see the scaffold below

```yaml
# title / one-liner / kind (bug, feature) / depends-on / requirements (the causes this settles) / id (back-annotated)
- title: example fix
  one-liner: what it changes
  kind: bug
  depends-on: []
  requirements: []
  id: ""
```

## Out of scope

%% @gummi: what this diagnosis deliberately won't explain or fix — each line is `- key: prose`

